So I think you want a ideally a single policy engine that is able to review all of your

00:54:23.497 --> 00:54:30.537
runtime activity to identify when things are going awry with misaligned intent for whatever

00:54:30.537 --> 00:54:34.777
reason and implement some type of blocking function or notifying and pulling in a human

00:54:34.936 --> 00:54:39.897
And then you'd want a secondary capability in that system to help you with optimization

00:54:39.897 --> 00:54:42.936
of workflows where applicable.

00:54:42.936 --> 00:54:49.737
Ideally, you know, that would be AI powered and ideally it'd operate in natural language

00:54:49.737 --> 00:54:52.216
to remove barriers between teams.

00:54:52.216 --> 00:54:57.176
But I think it's underlined by the idea of, I need very rich observability.

00:54:57.176 --> 00:55:01.657
I also need some type of LLM as a judge or AI to govern me.

00:55:01.657 --> 00:55:11.576
And then in the end to cap it off, I also want some type of optimization engine, something

00:55:11.576 --> 00:55:14.456
that's looking at it though, and can think outside the box.

00:55:17.816 --> 00:55:18.537
Anything else?

00:55:20.936 --> 00:55:27.576
I think the most effective feedback here could be where human feedback is concentrated.

00:55:27.737 --> 00:55:33.336
So let's say agentic AI has done a certain task and it has a confidence level as low

00:55:33.336 --> 00:55:34.377
or it's uncertain.

00:55:35.017 --> 00:55:37.657
I think that's the feedback we should be more focused on.

00:55:37.657 --> 00:55:42.777
So you should be looking at it constantly, you know, like a security, you know, you can

00:55:42.777 --> 00:55:44.856
constantly keep updating your cyber security policy.

00:55:44.856 --> 00:55:47.897
So same way as feedback, you have to constantly keep checking.

00:55:47.897 --> 00:55:52.856
And the beauty of agentic AI is it's able to tell the confidence of its answers.

00:55:52.856 --> 00:55:55.897
So in my case, it's able to tell the confidence of its answers.

00:55:55.897 --> 00:56:01.417
So anywhere the confidence is, let's say, as per company policy, that for cases related

00:56:01.417 --> 00:56:05.096
to accounts payable, confidence has to be minimum, let's say 99%.

00:56:05.657 --> 00:56:07.257
Anything below that, you need a human check.

00:56:07.257 --> 00:56:11.737
So I think that's a good way of, you know, making sure those feedback loops work.

00:56:12.297 --> 00:56:17.176
So it's alignment of this is not a one time, but you have to constantly keep working on

00:56:17.176 --> 00:56:17.737
it.

00:56:17.737 --> 00:56:22.377
So it's not a one time activity because your vendors are changing, your suppliers are changing,

00:56:22.377 --> 00:56:24.696
your customers needs are changing.

00:56:24.777 --> 00:56:27.976
So the agentic AI tool has to change accordingly.

00:56:27.976 --> 00:56:29.417
So keep working on it.

00:56:29.417 --> 00:56:30.216
That's how I would say.

00:56:30.216 --> 00:56:33.017
So you just govern the plan and not the output.

00:56:33.017 --> 00:56:33.976
That's how I would like to put it.

00:56:35.737 --> 00:56:37.176
